From: Angelpro09xd <167892325+Angelpro09xd@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sapphire-0291: USB Ethernet: RX stays armed when the TRB write-back is late

The PC -> phone direction died under load while phone -> PC kept going (30 MB copies out of the phone
worked, into it never). The trace showed why: an RX completion event whose TRB still had HWO set
(the controller's write-back not visible yet) was taken for a late event and dropped, after the
event had already marked the transfer inactive. Nothing armed RX again: the controller NAKed every
bulk OUT, the PC's cdc_ether timed out after 5 s and usbipd gave the device up ("late rx" counted
one per dead link). The write-back is now waited for (up to 1 ms); when it never comes RX is
armed again at once (that one frame is lost, TCP sends it again); and ud_watch arms RX
whenever nothing is armed at all.
---
 bsd/dev/sweet_usb.c | 28 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/bsd/dev/sweet_usb.c b/bsd/dev/sweet_usb.c
index 9f0b9ac..f4f919c 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_usb.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_usb.c
@@ -606,8 +606,23 @@ ud_rx_done(void)
 {
 	volatile uint32_t *t = (volatile uint32_t *)(ud.dma + UD_TRB_RX);
 	ud_sync(UD_TRB_RX, 16);
+	/*
+	 * 0291: the completion event can come before the controller's write-back of the TRB is visible
+	 * (HWO still set). Returning there left RX unarmed for good -- the event had already marked the
+	 * transfer inactive, so ud_watch did not look at it either -- and every bulk OUT from the host
+	 * was NAKed from then on: the PC -> phone direction of the link died ("late rx" went up by one
+	 * each time). Wait for the write-back; if HWO stays set the controller finished the transfer
+	 * without writing the TRB back (that frame is lost): arm RX again at once (ud_rx_arm ends a
+	 * transfer the controller still holds first).
+	 */
+	for (int i = 0; (t[3] & TRB_HWO) && i < 100; i++) {
+		delay(10);
+		ud_sync(UD_TRB_RX, 16);
+	}
 	if (t[3] & TRB_HWO) {
-		ud.stale_rx++;          /* a late event for a frame ud_watch already took */
+		ud.stale_rx++;
+		ut("RXS", t[3], t[2]);
+		ud_rx_arm();
 		return;
 	}
 	uint32_t len = UD_FRAME_MAX - (t[2] & 0xffffff);
@@ -947,6 +962,17 @@ ud_watch(void)
 	 * until usbipd gave the device up, while the phone's own frames kept going out. End the
 	 * transfer and arm it again; on a link that is merely idle that costs nothing.
 	 */
+	/* 0291: configured and no RX transfer at all (nothing armed): arm it */
+	static unsigned rx_unarmed;
+	if (!ud.xfer_active[EP_RX] && !(rt[3] & TRB_HWO)) {
+		if (++rx_unarmed >= 2) {
+			rx_unarmed = 0;
+			ut("RXU", (uint32_t)ud.rx_frames, rt[3]);
+			ud_rx_arm();
+		}
+	} else {
+		rx_unarmed = 0;
+	}
 	static unsigned rx_silent;
 	if (ud.xfer_active[EP_RX] && (rt[3] & TRB_HWO) && ud.rx_frames == ud.watch_rx) {
 		if (++rx_silent >= 4) {
